cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Molecular Animation, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "Molecular Animation: scientific protein and molecule animation in Blender"
abstract: >-
  An open-source Python framework and Blender 5.2 pipeline that turns a
  scientific brief and PDB/mmCIF or AlphaFold structures into honest,
  beautiful molecular animation: scripted scenes, rendered takes, labelled
  and clean MP4/WebM films with posters, and a production record that tags
  every beat as experimental, simulation-derived or illustrative. Thermal
  and Brownian motion is modelled at literature rates. The pipeline can be
  driven by an AI agent (Claude Code through Blender MCP) or by hand.
authors:
  - name: AmadeusBio.ai
    website: "https://www.amadeusbio.ai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AmadeusBio-ai/Molecular_Animation"
